<blockquote class="uncited"><div>SO....for those (still) looking at this thread; here's what to take-away:<br><br>- Adding your ID to every channel makes for a messy codeplug.<br>- Be sure to double-check which DMR ID you enter in the File Menu -&gt; Settings -&gt; DMR ID and callsign. (The callsign is NOT what is transmitted to the Network; just your ID (number).)<br><br>es vy 73 om's de "baab" w9ya</div></blockquote>I agree that the take-away from the most recent posts to this thread is that double check the Digital ID that you enter for any typos or mistakes.<br><br>However and on the contrary, entering the Digital ID to every channel, while unnecessary, did help to lead us to the conclusion that the error was in the master entry of the Digital ID.  There was nothing messy about it.  I will of course, remove them from each channel now that the master Digital ID is correct.<br><br>So, again, thank you W9YA for your sample codeplug and for your edification here are the only changes I made to it:<br><br>1) DMR ID and callsign: Enter my callsign and Radio (Digital) ID<br><br>2) Contacts -&gt; Digital Contacts: I added additional TalkGroups that I use<br><br>3) TG Lists: I modified 1 of your analog and 6 of your digital lists<br><br>4) Zones: I modified 1 of your analog and 3 of your digital zones<br><br>5) Channels: I modified 3 of your analog channels to the specifications of the 3 PAPA System analog repeaters that can be hit from my home and 6 of your digital channels to the specifications of the 3 PAPA System digital repeaters that can be hit from my home (1 each for Slot 1 and Slot 2). I am a member of the PAPA System which has repeaters throughout Southern California and Southern Nevada.<br><br>Now that I have it working, I am going to go through and rip out the other information that is personal to your usage and add the remainder of my RD-5R codeplug information that adds my personal usage, such as the addition of GMRS repeater and simplex and MURS simplex frequencies and 2 meter and 70 cms repeaters and simplex frequencies so that it will complete my DM-5R codeplug.<br><br>Thank you again!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1890">W7ML</a> — Wed Jun 14, 2023 10:30 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
